The Real Question
You asked: "Should I enhance the code further, or focus on what's around it?"
The answer depends on what gets you a thesis. A thesis is judged on evidence, not features.
What Gets You a Thesis	What Doesn't
"I ran 50 experiments proving my plan beats manual tuning by 40%" ✅	"I rewrote PipelineStageManager to support 17 parallelism types" ❌
"Ablations show profiling improves ranking accuracy by 35%" ✅	"I added FP8 support" ❌
"It scales from 4 to 12 GPUs with 82% efficiency" ✅	"I added sequence parallelism" ❌
"Convergence matches single-GPU within 1%" ✅	"I rewrote the cost model with 12 terms" ❌
Reviewers judge experiments. They don't judge code completeness.
