Priority 2: Larger Models (1 week)
bash launch_nodes.sh ... --auto --layers 24 --hidden 1024 --seq 512 --batch 16
Deliverable: Throughput scaling with model size.
Priority 3: Ablations (3–4 days)
Small code changes:
- Comment out profiler → use synthetic values
- Comment out pruning rules → see if it picks bad plans
- Force pp=1 or tp=1 → show all three matter
Deliverable: Table showing ranking accuracy with each component disabled.
Priority 4: Scalability (3–4 days)
bash launch_nodes.sh node18 node20 --auto  # 4 GPUs
bash launch_nodes.sh node18 node15 node16 --auto  # 6 GPUs
bash launch_nodes.sh node18 node15 node16 node19 --auto  # 8 GPUs
Deliverable: Speedup plot.
Priority 5: Convergence (2–3 days)
Run 100 steps, log loss. Compare single-GPU vs. 12-GPU.
Priority 6: Writing (3–4 weeks)
Chapters 1–6. This is what makes it a thesis.
